  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222163_Start Network Dyer Season Flood Anticipatory Action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Five districts are among flood prone zones in Somalia and El Ni&amp;#241;o is also forecasted to intensity the risk between October-December 2023; and Flooding from the Somali rivers (Shabelle and Juba rivers) can cause a lot of damage to the human lifestyle and environment, especially affecting displaced population settled in fragile shelters and in sites with no water drainage systems.
 
 Some flooding has now happened, so the nature of the project is AWD/Cholera and Malaria anticipatory action before the peak period as the floods are persisting. The planned interventions with this funding prior to forecasted AWD/Cholera and Malaria will prevent or mitigate negative impacts on vulnerable communities before they become severe by equipping households to undertake preventative measures.</narrative>
  </description>
